Reporting a suspected adverse drug reaction (synthetic case).

Patient: 64-year-old woman, 72 kg, history of hypertension and osteoarthritis.
Suspect drug: Carditol 40 mg tablets, 40 mg once daily, oral. Started 20 Apri=
l 2025.
Reaction: on 28 April 2025 she developed swelling of the lips and tongue with=
 difficulty swallowing (angioedema). No urticaria. She attended the emergency=
 department, received intramuscular adrenaline and hydrocortisone, and was ob=
served overnight.
Carditol was stopped on 28 April 2025. Symptoms resolved fully by the next da=
y. She has been advised not to take ACE-inhibitor-class medicines again.
Concomitant: atorvastatin 20 mg nightly. Outcome: recovered. Causality (my as=
sessment): probable.

Dr. A. Mecommet, GP, United Kingdom.
